 describe("dashboard presenter", () => {

codex
Findings from the review were all fixed.

1. The shared dashboard contract did not actually prevent advisory copy from entering the public display, so a future snapshot could violate the story’s fact-only doctrine despite the presenter tests. I added a contract-level guard in [dashboard-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/contracts/dashboard-snapshot.js#L1) and coverage in [dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs#L1).

2. App-level metadata was coupled to the dashboard feature through the root layout, which made the feature own global metadata instead of route-level metadata. I restored generic root metadata in [layout.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/layout.tsx#L1) and left the public-route metadata on the page feature.

3. The review/documentation state was inconsistent with the implementation: the story artifact and sprint tracker were still at review status even after the code passed the gate. I synced both to `done` in [1-3-render-the-overall-departure-picture.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/1-3-render-the-overall-departure-picture.md#L1) and [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml#L46).

I also had to tighten the smoke test in [startup-smoke.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/smoke/startup-smoke.test.mjs#L63) so it checks public-facing copy rather than tripping over the new banned-terms regex source.

Verification passed with `npm run validate` (`lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`). The story is now reviewed, fixed, and marked `done`.
