 ### Implementation Plan
 
-- Extend the current dashboard snapshot and presenter so nearby-mode comparison becomes a first-class part of the public display model.
-- Replace the summary placeholder in the lower grid with dedicated mode-summary components while keeping the future map slot intact for Story 1.5.
-- Lock the story down with contract/presenter tests and smoke checks that enforce fact-only copy, passive public rendering, and venue-specific shared readability.
+- Extend the dashboard snapshot contract with normalized nearby-mode items and presenter-facing state labels while keeping the public display fact-only.
+- Replace the summary placeholder with dedicated shared-reading mode-summary components and preserve the map frame as a reserved Story 1.5 slot.
+- Lock the work with unit and smoke assertions, then clear the repo validation gate (`lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`, `validate`) before marking review-ready.
 
 ### Completion Notes List
 
-- Created comprehensive story context for `1-4-show-nearby-mode-summaries-for-shared-reading`.
-- Added explicit guardrails around contract extension, presenter evolution, nearby-mode component boundaries, CSS-only implementation, and non-interactive public-display behavior.
-- Incorporated Story 1.3 handoff details so implementation starts from the existing reserved summary region instead of redesigning the dashboard shell.
-- Kept scope disciplined by excluding map work, live data refresh, trend, degraded-source handling, and device-verification work reserved for later stories.
-- Included current official-source sanity checks for Next.js, React, and Node.js so the dev agent can continue on the existing runtime baseline with confidence.
