+# Story 1.5: Anchor the Display with a Fixed Local Map
+
+Status: ready-for-dev
+
+<!-- Note: Validation is optional. Run validate-create-story for quality check before dev-story. -->
+
+## Story
+
+As a visitor,
+I want a fixed Royal Institution map anchor,
+so that I can understand nearby relevance and local spatial context without using an interactive map.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+1. Given the public display is rendering normally, when a visitor looks at the map area, then the Royal Institution anchor and selected nearby nodes are visible, and the map supports locality without becoming an exploratory city map.
+2. Given the map is part of the one-screen departure picture, when a visitor reads it with the rest of the display, then it reinforces the local from-here-now understanding, and it does not introduce route lines, turn-by-turn behavior, or route-planning affordances.
+3. Given the preferred map layer or enrichment cannot be shown, when the map area falls back to a simplified state, then a restrained fallback-map behavior preserves the Royal Institution anchor and local context, and the public screen remains usable and calm rather than blank or broken.
+
+## Tasks / Subtasks
+
+- [ ] Replace the reserved map placeholder with a real fixed local-map frame inside the existing dashboard feature boundary. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Keep [page.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/(public)/page.tsx) thin and continue composing the public display through `src/features/dashboard/*` rather than moving feature logic into the route. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Replace the `"Local frame"` reserved region in [DashboardScreen.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardScreen.tsx) with a dedicated `LocalMapFrame` component while preserving the existing header-first, modes-second, map-third reading order. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Keep the public route passive and non-interactive; no pan, zoom, hover tools, buttons, links, route affordances, or planner-like controls may appear on the map surface. (AC: 1, 2)
+- [ ] Extend the dashboard snapshot contract, fixture, and presenter to carry explicit local-map data plus fallback-state information. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Add a normalized `localMap` structure to [dashboard-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/contracts/dashboard-snapshot.js) with fields for map title, venue anchor, selected nearby nodes, optional corridor or locality emphasis, and a map state such as `default` or `fallback`. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Update [overall-departure-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/data/overall-departure-snapshot.js) to provide fixture-backed Royal Institution map data and a calm fallback variant without depending on live providers yet. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Update [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js) so components receive display-ready locality labels and fallback copy rather than raw map data. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+- [ ] Implement a restrained fixed local-map component that reads as architectural framing rather than interactive cartography. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Add `src/features/dashboard/components/LocalMapFrame.tsx` to render the Royal Institution anchor, selected nearby nodes, and any minimal locality-emphasis treatment approved by the UX spec. (AC: 1, 2)
+  - [ ] Use simple in-app rendering primitives such as semantic HTML, SVG, and custom CSS for the map frame instead of introducing a mapping library or external tile dependency. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Support both the default framed-map view and the simplified fallback-map view so the screen remains spatially useful even when enrichment is unavailable. (AC: 1, 3)
+- [ ] Preserve calm hierarchy and anti-planner doctrine while adding locality cues. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Keep the map visually secondary to the atmospheric header while still making the Royal Institution anchor and nearby nodes easy to identify at close reading distance. (AC: 1, 2)
+  - [ ] Avoid generic citywide treatment, dense cartographic labeling, route lines, turn-by-turn cues, or any suggestion that the display can be explored like a map application. (AC: 1, 2)
+  - [ ] Use custom CSS only in [globals.css](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/globals.css) to create the framed-map treatment, restrained overlays, and fallback-state styling that fit the established public-display palette. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+- [ ] Add tests that lock in the map contract, fallback behavior, and doctrine boundaries. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Extend [dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs) to cover approved local-map states, normalized node data, and presenter output for both normal and fallback map variants. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
+  - [ ] Extend [startup-smoke.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/smoke/startup-smoke.test.mjs) so the public route is required to render the Royal Institution map anchor, selected locality cues, and a passive non-interactive map region. (AC: 1, 2)
+  - [ ] Keep tests compatible with the existing `npm run validate` gate and avoid brittle visual snapshot testing or browser-only map assumptions. (AC: 1, 2, 3)
