     1	# Story 1.5: Anchor the Display with a Fixed Local Map
     2	
     3	Status: done
     4	
     5	<!-- Note: Validation is optional. Run validate-create-story for quality check before dev-story. -->
     6	
     7	## Story
     8	
     9	As a visitor,
    10	I want a fixed Royal Institution map anchor,
    11	so that I can understand nearby relevance and local spatial context without using an interactive map.
    12	
    13	## Acceptance Criteria
    14	
    15	1. Given the public display is rendering normally, when a visitor looks at the map area, then the Royal Institution anchor and selected nearby nodes are visible, and the map supports locality without becoming an exploratory city map.
    16	2. Given the map is part of the one-screen departure picture, when a visitor reads it with the rest of the display, then it reinforces the local from-here-now understanding, and it does not introduce route lines, turn-by-turn behavior, or route-planning affordances.
    17	3. Given the preferred map layer or enrichment cannot be shown, when the map area falls back to a simplified state, then a restrained fallback-map behavior preserves the Royal Institution anchor and local context, and the public screen remains usable and calm rather than blank or broken.
    18	
    19	## Tasks / Subtasks
    20	
