codex
Findings were fixed in place. The review started with three medium issues and all three are now closed:

- Fallback state was not enforced by the shared contract, so `state: "fallback"` could render without any fallback explanation. Fixed in [dashboard-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/contracts/dashboard-snapshot.js#L118) and covered by new contract assertions in [dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs#L278).
- The map intro preferred locality-emphasis copy even in fallback mode, so the simplified-state explanation could be hidden from the main reading path. Fixed in [LocalMapFrame.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/LocalMapFrame.tsx#L24).
- The fallback graphic still rendered the default corridor overlay, so the “simplified” state was not actually simplified. Fixed in [LocalMapFrame.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/LocalMapFrame.tsx#L71), with executable guardrails extended in [startup-smoke.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/smoke/startup-smoke.test.mjs#L111).

I also updated the story and sprint tracking to `done` in [1-5-anchor-the-display-with-a-fixed-local-map.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/1-5-anchor-the-display-with-a-fixed-local-map.md#L3) and [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml#L48).

Verification passed: `npm run validate` completed successfully. Residual risk is low; the only notable limitation is that the local `vitest-lite` harness still constrains direct TSX component execution from the existing `.mjs` unit suite, so part of the component fallback guard remains source-level in smoke coverage rather than a dedicated rendered TSX unit test.
