    17	3. Given the display is viewed on a secondary desktop-sized layout around `1024px+`, when the public route adapts to that width, then the core departure picture remains usable and location-specific, and the design does not collapse into a mobile, touch-first, or route-planner pattern.
    18	4. Given the implemented display is reviewed for UX verification obligations, when validation is run, then real-device display checks, contrast validation, and shared-readability expectations are represented directly in the work, and verification is not left implicit for a later phase.
    19	
