Implemented Story 1.6 end to end and moved it to `review`.

The public screen keeps the same canonical composition, with venue-sized layout hooks added in [DashboardScreen.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardScreen.tsx#L50) and responsive hardening in [globals.css](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/globals.css#L42) plus the new breakpoint/compact-height rules in [globals.css](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/globals.css#L493). The compact-height path now trims secondary support detail before primary hierarchy, preserves the header -> modes -> map order, and avoids any mobile/planner-style reflow below the supported desktop floor.

I added smoke coverage for the venue-sized pillars and verification artifact in [startup-smoke.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/smoke/startup-smoke.test.mjs#L136), and added explicit UX verification evidence in [1-6-display-verification-notes.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/1-6-display-verification-notes.md#L1). The story record and sprint status were updated in [1-6-verify-the-primary-display-on-real-venue-sized-surfaces.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/1-6-verify-the-primary-display-on-real-venue-sized-surfaces.md#L3) and [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml).

